 set is the UNION of ticket_ids across every review backing each emitted candidate (all _unique_reviews(reviews_for_norm) for fire; all silent reviews for no_fire), not one ticket per candidate, so escaped_defect stays byte-identical to the eager union.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.13,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_fire_rows computes escaped_defect via any(_escaped(review) for review in _unique_reviews(reviews_for_norm)) (fixture_selection.py:263-264)","_no_fire_rows computes it via any(_escaped(review) for review in silent) over all silent reviews (fixture_selection.py:299)","Plan says 'defer state compilation until a review is about to become an emitted candidate, so only the small candidate-referenced ticket set pays the cost' without noting the multi-review union"],"finding":"Option A's lazy compile scope is under-specified: escaped_defect is a set-union over ALL reviews backing each emitted candidate, not one ticket per candidate, so 'candidate-referenced tickets' must be the union of ticket_ids across every review contributing to an emitted candidate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f45f5e583622b7b7b","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, Option A; AC1","norm_id":"n42585b6b4a44098a","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A candidate norm backed by many reviews across many tickets; lazily compiling only the representative review's ticket would drop escaped_defect signals from the other backing reviews and change the rank tiebreak"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In Option A, state that after the candidate set is fixed, ticket_state is compiled for the union of ticket_ids over all reviews backing each emitted candidate (matching the current any(_escaped(...)) union in _fire_rows/_no_fire_rows), then escaped_defect is recomputed over that set.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","a