isely whether close_class==plan_defect and inbound caused_by are ANDed on a single ticket or each independently promotes, and align the Problem wording with AC3.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Problem: 'close_class == \"plan_defect\" and any inbound caused_by link'","AC3: 'a ticket closed plan_defect, and a ticket named by an inbound caused_by, both still rank-promote'"],"finding":"The definition of escaped_defect is stated ambiguously: the Problem section says it 'needs just two things: close_class == plan_defect AND any inbound caused_by link' (conjunction on one ticket), but AC3 describes two SEPARATE tickets that each rank-promote ('a ticket closed plan_defect, AND a ticket named by an inbound caused_by, both still rank-promote').","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fec8e59ab31769cdf","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Problem section ('needs just two things') vs AC3","norm_id":"n1bf2db5e207f8b5c","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If escaped_defect is a conjunction (both conditions on one ticket) the AC3 fixtures (two independent tickets) would not both promote; if it is a disjunction the Problem wording is wrong. The implementer building the batched index / lazy check needs to know whether to AND or OR the two signals."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Quote the actual escaped_defect(state) predicate from labels.py (e.g. 'returns True if close_class==\"plan_defect\" OR the ticket has an inbound caused_by edge') and phrase both the Problem note and AC3 to match it verbatim.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_